---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import P from "../components/P.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import spine from "../data/sicily-spine.json";
---
<Base title="The Mazza Name Line" eyebrow="Piedimonte Etneo, from about 1815"
      dek="On the morning this archive was built the Mazza name reached back four generations and stopped at a man with no dates. It now runs seven, and every step in Sicily is a document.">

  <section class="blk">
    <p class="lede">The archive opened with an embarrassment: <strong>the family took its name from
    its shallowest line.</strong> The Mazza of Piedimonte Etneo could be followed back four
    generations to a <P n="Rosario Mazza" /> about whom exactly one thing was asserted — that he
    fathered Salvatore — while the Calabrian <a href={u("/briatico/")}>Prostamo</a> ran nine
    generations to 1697.</p>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem">That is no longer true. On <strong>10 September
    2026</strong> the Sicilian registers gave up Salvatore's act of birth, and with it his father's
    age, his father's street, and his father's father.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">The act that did it</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.4rem">Piedimonte Etneo, Nati 1873, atto 3</h2>
    <div class="hero-plate" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
      <img src={u("/plates/act3-salvatore-mazza.jpg")} alt="Piedimonte Etneo birth register 1873, act 3" />
      <div>
        <blockquote style="margin:0 0 .9rem">…è comparso <strong>Rosario Mazza di Mariano</strong>,
        di anni <strong>ventotto</strong>, bracciante, qui domiciliato, il quale mi ha presentato un
        bambino di sesso maschile che dichiara essergli nato <strong>il giorno cinque corrente
        Gennaro</strong> alle ore sette antemeridiane, dalla di lui moglie <strong>Leonarda Bonanno
        di Gaetano</strong>, seco lui domiciliata nella casa di sua abitazione sita in questo Comune
        <strong>Contrada Terremorte</strong>, al quale figlio dichiara di dare il nome di
        <strong>Salvadore</strong>.</blockquote>
        <p><strong>Three things in one sentence.</strong> Salvatore Mazza was born on
        <strong>5 January 1873</strong> — not 1879, as the family tree has always said. His father
        Rosario was <strong>twenty-eight</strong>, which puts Rosario's own birth about 1844.
        And Rosario is <strong>«di Mariano»</strong> — son of a <strong>Mariano Mazza</strong> whom
        nothing in this archive had ever named.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:.8rem" class="small">Archivio di Stato di Catania, Stato civile
        italiano, Piedimonte Etneo, Nati 1873, atto 3 — Antenati <code>an_ua83486</code>, images 3–4.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <h2>The line, generation by generation</h2>
    <div class="stack" style="margin-top:24px">
      {spine.map((g) => (
        <div class="linerow">
          <div>
            <div class="lab">Generation {g.gen}</div>
            <div style="font-size:24px;line-height:1.15;margin-top:8px">{g.name}</div>
            <div class="mono" style="margin-top:6px;color:var(--ink-3)">
              {g.born !== "—" ? g.born : ""}{g.died && g.died !== "—" ? ` – ${g.died}` : ""}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            {g.bornNote !== "—" && <p class="qw">{g.bornNote}</p>}
            {g.spouse !== "—" && (
              <p class="qn" style="margin-top:10px">Married <strong>{g.spouse}</strong>.
              {g.spouseNote !== "—" ? " " + g.spouseNote : ""}</p>
            )}
            <p class="ab"><strong>Source:</strong> {g.source}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="lab">How the tree was wrong, and why it mattered</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.4rem">Six years, and eight wasted registers</h2>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1rem">
      <p>The family tree gives Salvatore Mazza as <strong>born 1879 at Piedimonte Etneo, died 1929 at
      Catania</strong>. Acting on that, this archive read the birth registers of Piedimonte Etneo for
      <strong>1875, 1876, 1877, 1878, 1879, 1880, 1881 and 1882</strong>, and those of Mascali and
      Giarre for 1879, and found no Salvatore Mazza in any of them.</p>
      <p>He was born in <strong>1873</strong>, six years earlier, and he died at
      <strong>Piedimonte Etneo</strong>, not Catania — in the frazione of <strong>Vena</strong>, at
      Contrada Grotta Nicodemo, on <strong>19 September 1929</strong>, aged fifty-six.</p>
      <p><strong>The lesson is about search strategy, not about the tree.</strong> Eight registers
      were read on the strength of one undocumented year. What actually broke it open was working
      from a <em>different</em> record — the Queensland death index, which gave Salvatore's son
      Rosario a birth year of 1899 and his wife her full name — and then finding the parish marriage
      of 1898 and the civil death act of 1929, each of which names Salvatore's parents. <strong>Three
      records converged on the man before the register was opened at the right page.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk" style="border-bottom:0">
    <div class="lab">And what it does to the hundred and ten</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.4rem">Mariano</h2>
    <p class="dek" style="margin-top:.9rem">The <a href={u("/components/")}>second component</a> of the
    family tree — the hundred and ten Piedimonte Etneo Mazza joined to this family by nothing — is
    headed by a <strong>Rosario Mazza born 1850</strong>, and it contains a
    <strong>Mariano Mazza</strong>.</p>
    <p class="dek" style="margin-top:1rem">The register now gives a <strong>Rosario Mazza born about
    1844</strong> whose father was <strong>Mariano</strong>. That is a second, independent
    correspondence on top of the Orazio one — and it is the strongest reason yet to think the two
    halves are one family. <strong>It is still not the document that joins them.</strong> What would
    do that is <strong>Rosario's own marriage act</strong>, which would name Mariano with an age and
    a wife. <a href={u("/open-questions/")}>The queue →</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
